{% set local_problem %}
<p>Scottsboro sits in a heavily wooded area with a mix of pine and hardwood trees. That means debris lands in your gutters year-round — pine needles in spring and summer, leaves in fall, and twigs and seeds in between.</p>

<p>When gutters clog, water overflows and heads straight for your foundation. Scottsboro's clay-heavy soil doesn't absorb that water well, so it pools around your home and eventually finds its way into basements and crawlspaces.</p>

<p>For vacation homeowners near Lake Guntersville, the stakes are even higher. Clogged gutters can cause damage while you're away — and you won't know until your next visit. Regular professional cleaning prevents these problems before they start.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We remove all debris by hand from inside your gutters — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are a common problem that homeowners miss when cleaning themselves.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system for problems: loose hangers, small leaks, rust spots, and fascia damage. For vacation homeowners, we can document everything with photos and send a detailed report.</p>
{% endset %}

